    turnFlow: 'Blinds. Deal 5. Betting round. Draw up to 4 cards. Final betting. Showdown. Altered rankings: Flush > Full House (flushes rarer in 32-card deck). A can be low: A-7-8-9-10 = valid straight. Suit ranking may tiebreak.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: '32-card Poker uses blinds instead of a separate ante action; forced bets are handled as part of the betting structure.',
      deal: 'The initial 5-card deal is handled by the dealer as part of setup, not as a player-triggered action.',
      reveal_market: 'This game does not use a face-up market; all cards come from a single stock.',
      buy_market: 'There is no market row to buy from in 32-card Poker.',
      buy_stock: 'Cards are drawn as part of the exchange draw, not bought individually from stock.',
      fold: 'Available during any betting round; a folded player is out for the rest of the hand.',
      check: 'Only legal when no bet has been opened in the current betting round.',
      call: 'Only legal when a bet or raise is outstanding; must match the full current bet.',
      bet: 'Only legal when there is no current open bet; sets the amount others must call or raise.',
      raise: 'Only legal when a bet or raise already exists; may be limited by house raise caps.',
      declare: 'There is no separate high/low declaration step; the single best high hand wins the pot at showdown.',
      reveal_hand: 'Triggered for all active players in the showdown phase.',
      award_pot: 'Dealer-only action in the showdown phase; flush ranks above full house and suit order may break exact ties.',
      play_card: '32-card Poker is a draw poker game; players do not play cards to a central trick or layout.',
      draw: 'Available once per hand during the draw phase after choosing discards; you may draw from zero up to four cards but must finish with exactly five cards.',
      discard: 'Available only in the draw phase before drawing; you may discard between zero and four cards and must keep at least one original card.',
      pass: 'Passing the betting action is represented by check; there is no separate pass action in this poker game.',
      bid: 'There is no contract or bid mechanic; betting uses bet, call, raise, check, and fold.',
      meld: '32-card Poker is not a rummy-style melding game; hands are evaluated as poker combinations only.',
      go_out: 'The hand ends at showdown after betting; there is no separate go-out action.',
    },
